  "result": "Perfect! \u2705 All 417 tests pass (402 existing + 15 new mergeCustomers tests).\n\n**`mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId)` added to `src/customers.js`:**\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Removes the `fromId` customer from the customers array\n- Reassigns all invoices with `fromId` as customerId to `intoId`\n- Returns `ok({ customers, invoices })` with the merged state\n- Both IDs are normalized (trimmed and uppercased)\n\n**Error handling:**\n- `SAME_CUSTOMER` \u2014 fromId and intoId are the same (after normalization)\n- `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` \u2014 either customer doesn't exist in the array\n\n**Immutability:**\n- Creates new arrays instead of mutating inputs\n- Preserves customer details for the `intoId` customer\n- Maps invoices to new objects when reassigning\n\n**Test coverage (15 new tests):**\n- Basic merge functionality\n- Invoice reassignment (single and multiple)\n- Unaffected invoices remain unchanged\n- Error cases (same customer, missing customers)\n- Normalization of IDs (case and whitespace)\n- Immutability verification\n- Large dataset handling (100+ invoices)\n- Empty invoice array\n- Customer details preservation\n\nAll invoicing features now complete: invoices, payments, terms, vouchers, discounts, VAT, reports (overdue, VAT summary, late fees), CSV export, multi-currency support, and customer merging.",
